+    // half of real Windows machines have; excluding it would keep applying a fixed haircut to
+    // every Office host, the exact failure the 63-name list had.
+    //
+    // Face names were then dropped EMPIRICALLY, not by guesswork: every candidate was measured
+    // with a three-baseline canvas width probe under stock Chrome on a real Windows host, and
+    // everything stock Chrome cannot resolve as a family was removed -- "Arial Bold",
+    // "Georgia Italic", "Segoe UI Semilight", "Sitka" and ~155 other faces. Keeping them would
+    // make the cross-OS path below claim fonts a real Windows machine reports absent.
